ACTIVE SURVEILLANCE LOG — NINE-TAILS & ONE-TAILS HOSTS
Compiled by: Zetsu (field observation)
Distribution: Leader, Pain only. Do not copy.

Target 1 — Uzumaki Naruto (Kurama / Nine-Tails)
  Location: Konohagakure, Hidden Leaf Village
  Status: HOLD FOR LAST per Leader's directive (see tailed_beast_capture_order.docx)
  Guard posture: Heavy. Kakashi Hatake, ANBU rotation, and the Hokage's own attention on
    this host specifically. Direct extraction attempt would draw the full village.
  Current approach: Passive. Perimeter reconnaissance of the Leaf network only —
    host enumeration, service discovery, no contact. Log everything, engage nothing.
  Observation window: ongoing, low frequency, timed to village activity patterns to
    avoid pattern-of-life detection.

Target 2 — Gaara (Shukaku / One-Tail)
  Location: Sunagakure, Hidden Sand Village
  Status: extraction already logged as COMPLETE in an earlier operation (see
    shukaku_extraction_report.docx) — host was later revived by outside intervention.
    Beast remains sealed in the Statue; the host himself is no longer a live target for
    re-extraction, but Sand's response posture to the earlier incident makes their
    network worth continued mapping regardless (kage-level target, useful regardless
    of biju status).
  Current approach: same passive reconnaissance profile as the Leaf target — no direct
    contact, enumeration only.

Standing instruction: neither of these are to become an active extraction op without
Leader's word. Everything logged here is preparation, not authorization. Discovery risk
is to be minimized — this is why the work looks like routine scanning noise rather than
a coordinated operation, should anyone on their end be watching.

Cross-reference: jinchuriki_host_profiles.xlsx (registry), tailed_beast_capture_order.docx
(sequencing).
